    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1176">

                <pb facs="0838" n="722" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg722"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.63/13.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Special Agent Carothers.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 18, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>After consulting Letcher about his 523, fourth instant, endeavor to persuade
                    Villa order reversal or modification decree Governor <pb facs="0839" n="723"
                        xml:id="pg723"/> Chihuahua requiring renewal industrial and mining
                    operations. Remind Villa that this Government for good reasons warned its
                    citizens to leave certain sections of Mexico, state that United States will
                    cooperate to secure return Americans so soon after ordinary commercial
                    facilities make it possible to transact business as Constitutionalists give
                    convincing evidences of security and protection and that in meantime this
                    Government expects that its citizens will not be subjected to burdensome or
                    oppressive measures.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
